From: =?UTF-8?q?Zal=C3=A1n=20Demeter?= <zalan.demeter@industreal.tech>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:03:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] GLES3: Compile tonemapping out of the scene shader for
 the linear tonemapper

apply_tonemapping() returns its input unchanged for TONEMAPPER_LINEAR, but the
scene shader still evaluates the tonemapper selection for every pixel. Only
define APPLY_TONEMAPPING when a non-linear tonemapper is in use. The output is
bit-identical; the variant without APPLY_TONEMAPPING already exists (it is used
when environment effects are applied in post).
---
 drivers/gles3/rasterizer_scene_gles3.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gles3/rasterizer_scene_gles3.cpp b/drivers/gles3/rasterizer_scene_gles3.cpp
index bf41012..9ce318f 100644
--- a/drivers/gles3/rasterizer_scene_gles3.cpp
+++ b/drivers/gles3/rasterizer_scene_gles3.cpp
@@ -2829,7 +2829,9 @@ void RasterizerSceneGLES3::render_scene(const Ref<RenderSceneBuffers> &p_render_
 			spec_constant_base_flags |= SceneShaderGLES3::USE_DEPTH_FOG;
 		}
 
-		if (!apply_environment_effects_in_post) {
+		// The linear tonemapper returns its input unchanged, so leave the tonemapping code out
+		// rather than branch on the tonemapper per pixel.
+		if (!apply_environment_effects_in_post && tonemap_ubo.tonemapper != int32_t(RSE::ENV_TONE_MAPPER_LINEAR)) {
 			spec_constant_base_flags |= SceneShaderGLES3::APPLY_TONEMAPPING;
 		}
 	}
